{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341177-fortress-in-the-dreams","id":341177,"title":"Fortress in the Dreams?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-15T13:55:38-08:00","id":341177,"title":"Fortress in the Dreams?","content":"So I reread <b>Changeling</b> corebook for the game I run. I'm on the Oneiromancy and it got me thinking - How cool would be to have a private fortress in the dreams to defend and expand? But then I understand that Dreams <b>are not</b> Astral Space, and they are not constant. In <b>Mage</b> you can change and develop Oneiros of character as it is mostly constant. In <b>Changeling</b>, every Dream is a new scenery, not connected with previous. So question is this: <b>How can I get my dreamed castle that will show up in my next few dreams and it would have sense to build it in details? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:11:39-08:00","id":341208,"title":"","content":"From what I understand from reading both the Changeling corebook and Astral Realms is that when the Changeling enters a dream it's usually with a purpose in mind. Typically, gathering Glamour, which requires a specific emotional state. They can't acquire it more than once from the same situation, ergo, they can't gather it more than once from the memory or dream of a situation either, so when gathering Glamour they go to different memories or dreams. A Mage would, upon entering the Oneiros, sort it into some kind of order- a path, a journey, a city, whatever. For a Mage, who tries to improve themselves, change their psyche, etc. there are static, set pieces to an Oneiros- for a Changeling, who's usually there to tweak a memory or gather Glamour, there doesn't need to be.<br /> <br /> So, perhaps the person this Changeling is pursuing has some knowledge of the Occult, and some knowledge of tricks like Memory Palaces and Lucid Dreaming. Putting those together, this mortal could prepare their mind against assault, and maybe set a mental 'trip wire' so that if they're sleeping when the Oneiros is entered, they begin to dream lucidly and can fight back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:17:57-08:00","id":341214,"title":"","content":"See Bastions from Dancers in the Dusk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:43:12-08:00","id":341543,"title":"","content":"^<br /> <br /> They're pretty much exactly what you want. Permanent (or semi-permanent) fortresses in dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}